{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"USN-8951-1","published":"2026-10-21T18:20:42Z","modified":"2026-10-22T04:42:58.035678055Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2020-22217","UBUNTU-CVE-2022-4904","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-69184","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-69186"],"upstream":["CVE-2020-22217","CVE-2022-4904","CVE-2026-69184","CVE-2026-69186","UBUNTU-CVE-2020-22217","UBUNTU-CVE-2022-4904","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-69184","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-69186"],"summary":"c-ares vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that c-ares incorrectly parsed certain SOA replies. A\nremote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause c-ares to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS\nand Ubuntu 18.04 LTS. (CVE-2020-22217)\n\nIt was discovered that c-ares incorrectly handled certain sortlist strings.\nA remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause c-ares to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary code. This issue\nonly affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2022-4904)\n\nIt was discovered that c-ares did not properly limit DNS compression\npointer hops or assembled name lengths when parsing DNS names. A remote\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause c-ares to use excessive\nresources, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-69184)\n\nIt was discovered that c-ares did not properly validate record count fields\nbefore allocating memory when parsing DNS responses. A remote attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause c-ares to use excessive resources,\nresulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS\nand Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-69186)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"c-ares","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/c-ares?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.10.0-3ubuntu0.2+esm4"}]}],"versions":["1.10.0-2","1.10.0-3","1.10.0-3ubuntu0.1","1.10.0-3ubuntu0.2","1.10.0-3ubuntu0.2+esm1","1.10.0-3ubuntu0.2+esm2","1.10.0-3ubuntu0.2+esm3"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"libc-ares2","binary_version":"1.10.0-3ubuntu0.2+esm4"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"CVE-2020-22217","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2022-4904","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2026-69184","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]}],"ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS"},"source":"https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-security-notices/blob/main/osv/usn/USN-8951-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"c-ares","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:18.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/c-ares?arch=source&distro=esm-infra%2Fbionic"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.14.0-1ubuntu0.2+esm3"}]}],"versions":["1.13.0-2","1.13.0-3","1.14.0-1","1.14.0-1ubuntu0.1","1.14.0-1ubuntu0.2","1.14.0-1ubuntu0.2+esm1","1.14.0-1ubuntu0.2+esm2"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro (Infra-only): https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"libc-ares2","binary_version":"1.14.0-1ubuntu0.2+esm3"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"CVE-2020-22217","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2026-69184","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]}],"ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:18.04:LTS"},"source":"https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-security-notices/blob/main/osv/usn/USN-8951-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"c-ares","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:20.04:LTS","purl":"pkg